        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: DeVry University, Chicago Public Schools, DeVry University Advantage Academy\n- Places: Chicago, Illinois\n- Topics: dual degree high schools, for-profit colleges, associate degrees\n\nFacts:\n- DeVry University was founded in 1931 as DeForest Training School.\n- DeVry University officially became DeVry University in 2002.\n- DeVry University is an American for-profit college.\n- DeVry University Advantage Academy is a 2-year dual degree high school located in Chicago, Illinois.\n- DeVry University Advantage Academy is operated through a partnership between Chicago Public Schools and DeVry University.\n- DeVry University Advantage Academy offers students the opportunity to graduate with a high school diploma and an associate degree in Networking System Administration or Web Graphic Design.",
